  "notes": "All 41 items on the list are recorded, across five sections (schoolwide centers, schoolwide programs, department-based labs, research groups, cross-university centers). The Idea Hub link is a school initiative to bring partners together, not a research group, and was left out. The Center for Health Data Science name is linked on the list to the BEDAC page (the address recorded); a separate link in the related-pages block points to https://www.bu.edu/sph/research/centers-and-groups/health-data-science-center/. Some entries (Framingham Heart Study, Grayken Center, Providence/Boston CFAR, PEPRec, Healthy Minds Network) are partner or external programs the list shows as SPH-linked. No leads or blurbs shown on the list. Left out because the directory already has them (9): Center on Emerging Infectious Diseases (target bu-ceid); Chronic Traumatic Encephalopathy (CTE) Center (target bu-cte); Clinical & Translational Science Institute (target bu-ctsi); Evans Center for Interdisciplinary Biomedical Research (target bu-evans-ibr); Framingham Heart Study; Global Development Policy Center (target bu-gdp); Institute for Global Sustainability (target bu-igs); Rafik B. Hariri Institute for Computational Science & Engineering (target bu-hariri); Sloane Epidemiology Center. Named on the pages but given no entry, because no lead or site of their own is shown (4): Emerging World Leaders; Black Women’s Health Study; Alzheimer’s Disease Research; Program on Reproductive Justice."
